    /// Use this endpoint to create, read, update and delete Individual expense entries.This endpoint provides access to individual expense entries with comprehensive details about expense types, amounts, locations, and related information.Expenses represent individual expense line items that can be of three types: Receipts (regular expenses with vendor information), Mileage (travel expenses with from/to locations and distance), and Per Diem (daily allowance expenses with quantity and rates).Each expense entry includes complete financial information with amounts in both division currency (DC) and foreign currency (FC), exchange rates, project associations, categorization, and approval workflow details.The endpoint provides enriched data including user names for all related personnel (claimant, creator, modifier), project descriptions, category descriptions, status descriptions, and expense type descriptions for better usability.Retrieving Expenses with Child Data:• Standard OData: GET /Expenses or GET /Expenses?$filter=Report eq guid&apos;{id}&apos; automatically includes child data• Child data (ExpenseLine and Waypoint) are loaded via subqueries for each expense• ExpenseLine - For Receipt type expenses (Type 1), single line with amount and category• Waypoint - For Mileage type expenses (Type 2), single location with coordinates• Per Diem expenses (Type 3) have no child dataExpense Types:• Type 1: Receipts - Standard expenses with vendor and receipt information, includes single ExpenseLine• Type 2: Mileage - Travel expenses with distance and location tracking, includes single Waypoint• Type 3: Per Diem - Daily allowance expenses with quantity-based calculationsStatus Values:• Status 1: Reviewed - Expense has been reviewed and approved• Status 2: Not reviewed - Expense awaiting review (default)• Status 3: Flagged - Expense requires attention or clarification• Status 4: Deleted - Expense marked for deletionAuthorization:• Users can only view and delete expenses they created• Report approvers can view and delete all expenses in reports they approve• Delete operations check creator ownership and report status• Expenses cannot be deleted if report status is Submitted, Approved, FinanceApproved, or ProcessedOperations supported:• GET: Retrieve expenses with filtering and sorting capabilities (includes child data)• POST: Create new expense entries with type-specific validation• PUT: Update existing expenses (amounts, descriptions, status, etc.)• DELETE: Delete expense entries (validates authorization and report status)• POST (Service Operation): DeleteExpenses - Bulk delete multiple expenses with authorization checksSpecial Features:• DeleteExpenses: Bulk delete with proper child data cleanup and detailed failure reporting• Type-specific validation for mileage and per diem expenses• Automatic currency conversion support• Project and category association for detailed reporting• Business Component (BC) pattern ensures data integrity and proper child deletionFor more information about the ExpenseManagement functionality in Exact Online, see Work with expense management.
